WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.486 --> 00:00:01.483
- What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:01.483 --> 00:00:02.486
It's Evan.

00:00:02.486 --> 00:00:04.189
My one word is believe
and I believe in people

00:00:04.189 --> 00:00:05.735
more than they believe in themselves

00:00:05.735 --> 00:00:07.731
and I want some of that
to rub off onto you

00:00:07.731 --> 00:00:09.870
so that you can take
that thing that's in here

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.356
and unleash it into the world

00:00:11.356 --> 00:00:12.715
so to help you on your journey,

00:00:12.715 --> 00:00:15.359
today we're continuing the
How Billionaires Think,

00:00:15.359 --> 00:00:18.890
Success Advice from the
Top Series, Volume Four,

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.170
and as always guys, as you're watching,

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.042
if you hear something that
really resonates with you

00:00:22.042 --> 00:00:23.387
make sure to put it in quotes

00:00:23.387 --> 00:00:24.858
and leave it in the comments below.

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:27.439
It will inspire other people,
but as you write it down

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:30.155
it's much more likely to
stick with yourself as well.

00:00:30.155 --> 00:00:30.988
Enjoy.

00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:42.164
- Every time's a perfect
time to start a business.

00:00:42.164 --> 00:00:43.923
There's no bad time.

00:00:43.923 --> 00:00:46.389
If you do the work, if
you do the preparation,

00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:48.196
you'll know when it's time

00:00:48.196 --> 00:00:50.517
and it doesn't mean that it
won't be a little bit scary

00:00:50.517 --> 00:00:52.767
but, you know, you'll know,

00:00:54.259 --> 00:00:56.977
and you don't have to quit the daytime job

00:00:56.977 --> 00:00:58.879
if you don't feel all that comfortable

00:00:58.879 --> 00:01:00.234
and you can give it a run at night,

00:01:00.234 --> 00:01:01.456
but whatever works for you.

00:01:01.456 --> 00:01:04.092
Now with the internet,

00:01:04.092 --> 00:01:05.668
you've got all the choices in the world

00:01:05.668 --> 00:01:07.960
and you can just go out
there and do your own thing

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:10.627
and set up a business part time.

00:01:16.819 --> 00:01:20.047
- We've had this tradition
for, I don't know,

00:01:20.047 --> 00:01:22.974
probably seven or eight
years at the company

00:01:22.974 --> 00:01:26.522
where every week we have a Q and A

00:01:26.522 --> 00:01:29.887
where our employees can
come and ask me any question

00:01:29.887 --> 00:01:31.386
that they want about what's going on

00:01:31.386 --> 00:01:33.911
and what the direction of the company is

00:01:33.911 --> 00:01:36.243
or questions or things that
they read about in the press

00:01:36.243 --> 00:01:39.000
or that their friends
that use the product,

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.199
what they're asking them,

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:44.171
and it's been this really
important tradition for us,

00:01:44.171 --> 00:01:47.401
both because we really believe
in openness and communication

00:01:47.401 --> 00:01:49.569
and that's kind of what
Facebook is all about,

00:01:49.569 --> 00:01:52.447
but it's also really important for me

00:01:52.447 --> 00:01:56.193
and for running the company
to be able to get feedback

00:01:56.193 --> 00:01:59.459
and to be able to learn
what's on people's minds,

00:01:59.459 --> 00:02:03.286
what our employees and folks
who are part of our team

00:02:03.286 --> 00:02:06.915
are thinking about, and a lot of the time

00:02:06.915 --> 00:02:09.056
there are good questions that people ask

00:02:09.056 --> 00:02:11.858
that change the way that we
think about what we're building

00:02:11.858 --> 00:02:14.086
and what we're here to do in the world

00:02:14.086 --> 00:02:16.616
that often make us go think and reevaluate

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:20.616
how we should be approaching
different problems.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.039
- There's a very thin dividing line

00:02:27.039 --> 00:02:28.858
between success and failure

00:02:28.858 --> 00:02:32.296
when you start a business from scratch,

00:02:32.296 --> 00:02:35.026
and if you don't have enough
money to pay the bills

00:02:35.026 --> 00:02:36.828
you go the wrong side
of that dividing line

00:02:36.828 --> 00:02:39.889
and if you can somehow get
enough money to pay the bills

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:43.722
you stay the right side
of that dividing line.

00:02:46.892 --> 00:02:51.701
I've always been running
faster than perhaps I should

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:54.848
and I have great difficulty
saying no to things

00:02:54.848 --> 00:02:57.552
so I keep on taking new things

00:02:57.552 --> 00:03:00.646
and we've just managed
to stay the right side

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:04.094
of the dividing line over
the last 50 years in business

00:03:04.094 --> 00:03:07.329
but equally in those early days

00:03:07.329 --> 00:03:09.149
when you're starting a business

00:03:09.149 --> 00:03:11.521
without any financial backing,

00:03:11.521 --> 00:03:14.183
it's easy to slip the wrong side

00:03:14.183 --> 00:03:18.429
and in fact, most entrepreneurs
do slip the wrong side

00:03:18.429 --> 00:03:22.666
and the important thing is
then just pick yourself up

00:03:22.666 --> 00:03:23.999
and start again.

00:03:25.356 --> 00:03:26.661
If it doesn't work at that time,

00:03:26.661 --> 00:03:30.828
keep going until you do
succeed and not to give up.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:40.572
- I have young filmmakers
come up to me and say

00:03:40.572 --> 00:03:43.671
give me some advice for doing this,

00:03:43.671 --> 00:03:47.445
and I say don't put
limitations on yourself.

00:03:47.445 --> 00:03:48.909
Other people will do that for you.

00:03:48.909 --> 00:03:49.987
Don't do it to yourself.

00:03:49.987 --> 00:03:53.969
Don't bet against yourself and take risks.

00:03:53.969 --> 00:03:56.523
NASA has this phrase that they like,

00:03:56.523 --> 00:04:01.435
failure is not an option, but
failure has to be an option

00:04:01.435 --> 00:04:05.120
in art and in exploration
because it's a leap of faith

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.908
and no important endeavor
that required innovation

00:04:08.908 --> 00:04:10.920
was done without risk.

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.826
You have to be willing
to take those risks.

00:04:13.826 --> 00:04:16.049
So, that's the thought
I would leave you with

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:20.132
is in whatever you're
doing, failure is an option

00:04:21.891 --> 00:04:23.224
but fear is not.

00:04:29.345 --> 00:04:32.589
- There's the Latin expression
which I think is great.

00:04:32.589 --> 00:04:36.079
I love it, was in the now very old movie

00:04:36.079 --> 00:04:39.040
called The Dead Poet's Society,

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.207
but the line of the movie was
carpe diem, seize the day.

00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:46.270
The opportunities are there,

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:49.156
but you got to reach out and pick 'em up.

00:04:49.156 --> 00:04:51.272
You got to grab at 'em.

00:04:51.272 --> 00:04:53.702
Some of you may have
already done that at the U,

00:04:53.702 --> 00:04:57.409
in your classes, in other
students that you met,

00:04:57.409 --> 00:05:01.029
in your extracurricular
activities, but grab them.

00:05:01.029 --> 00:05:02.713
Don't be afraid to make a mistake,

00:05:02.713 --> 00:05:06.332
'cause you know what you can
do if you grab the wrong one?

00:05:06.332 --> 00:05:08.756
Drop it and pick up another one.

00:05:08.756 --> 00:05:09.991
It's okay.

00:05:09.991 --> 00:05:11.158
Seize the day.

00:05:12.517 --> 00:05:15.184
I think back of all of the luck,

00:05:16.594 --> 00:05:19.194
but also the times that
were in front of me

00:05:19.194 --> 00:05:20.611
to seize the day.

00:05:22.329 --> 00:05:25.114
I don't know what got me to
drop out of business school

00:05:25.114 --> 00:05:27.041
and come to Microsoft.

00:05:27.041 --> 00:05:30.180
My parents thought I was a whack job.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:32.611
Neither one of them graduated college

00:05:32.611 --> 00:05:36.133
and they thought this
was really a wild idea.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:37.523
I was lucky.

00:05:37.523 --> 00:05:38.940
I seized the day.

00:05:39.914 --> 00:05:43.581
Microsoft, one day some
guys fly in from IBM

00:05:45.888 --> 00:05:48.664
and all of a sudden we figure
out we could actually provide

00:05:48.664 --> 00:05:50.774
all the software they need

00:05:50.774 --> 00:05:54.706
for this thing that became
the personal computer.

00:05:54.706 --> 00:05:57.746
People, Bill, Paul, they had the wisdom

00:05:57.746 --> 00:06:02.355
to seize the day when that
opportunity presented itself,

00:06:02.355 --> 00:06:04.487
and yet when you think
of all the opportunities,

00:06:04.487 --> 00:06:07.221
when I think back of all
the opportunities I've had,

00:06:07.221 --> 00:06:09.561
the one that was most important

00:06:09.561 --> 00:06:13.033
was an opportunity I got in 1969

00:06:13.033 --> 00:06:15.342
sitting in my junior high school class.

00:06:15.342 --> 00:06:17.415
I was in a public junior high,

00:06:17.415 --> 00:06:21.582
not very stimulated at the
time and over the loudspeaker

00:06:23.276 --> 00:06:26.176
they said a private
high school in our area

00:06:26.176 --> 00:06:27.822
that I'd never heard of

00:06:27.822 --> 00:06:31.448
was giving scholarship tests that weekend.

00:06:31.448 --> 00:06:33.226
I told my mother I wanted to take them.

00:06:33.226 --> 00:06:35.961
She said that's fine, as
long as you get a scholarship

00:06:35.961 --> 00:06:38.457
because we can't afford to send you there,

00:06:38.457 --> 00:06:41.032
but that's really where
I got switched out,

00:06:41.032 --> 00:06:44.248
switched on in math,
switched on personally,

00:06:44.248 --> 00:06:49.182
energized in a way that
never could be turned back

00:06:49.182 --> 00:06:52.796
and I'm very thankful
for that opportunity.

00:06:52.796 --> 00:06:56.230
Yes, there's a lot of luck in opportunity,

00:06:56.230 --> 00:06:59.360
but there's a lot of seizing the day

00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:04.083
and I encourage you all to
reach out and carpe diem,

00:07:04.083 --> 00:07:08.250
really seize the opportunities
that are in front of you.

00:07:14.095 --> 00:07:17.913
- I don't wish to alienate people here

00:07:17.913 --> 00:07:21.330
with what I'm about to say, but you know,

00:07:22.537 --> 00:07:25.037
your destiny is in your hands.

00:07:28.529 --> 00:07:30.946
I succeeded because I had to.

00:07:32.825 --> 00:07:35.658
No one sorted anything out for me.

00:07:37.173 --> 00:07:41.266
I didn't ask out to any
government and said pretty please,

00:07:41.266 --> 00:07:45.394
find me some work, please,
and do something for me,

00:07:45.394 --> 00:07:49.382
because it was a waste of
bloody time, simply that,

00:07:49.382 --> 00:07:51.960
a waste of time, and if I
was going to do something

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:53.350
I had to do it myself.

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:57.886
That's it, and I would say
to every one of you here

00:07:57.886 --> 00:08:02.537
don't sit around relying upon
magically some government

00:08:02.537 --> 00:08:04.253
going to create an environment

00:08:04.253 --> 00:08:05.883
that's going to make it easy for you

00:08:05.883 --> 00:08:07.466
to find work and find jobs.

00:08:07.466 --> 00:08:10.582
You've got to go out there
and fight for it yourself.

00:08:10.582 --> 00:08:14.749
I'm sorry to say I can't give
you any other form of advice.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:18.722
If you want something
bad enough, you do it

00:08:18.722 --> 00:08:21.509
and if you look at some of these wannabes

00:08:21.509 --> 00:08:26.230
that make themselves
television stars and pop stars

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.899
and all that type of stuff,

00:08:27.899 --> 00:08:31.040
they have a desire to want to be famous

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.643
and they don't stop until
they're recognized and they do,

00:08:34.643 --> 00:08:36.909
and half the people you see
on television these days

00:08:36.909 --> 00:08:39.400
in the entertainment industry

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:42.786
are those that had a
determination they wanted to do it

00:08:42.786 --> 00:08:44.508
and I'll a little rider to that,

00:08:44.508 --> 00:08:46.925
none of them can bloody sing.

00:08:50.319 --> 00:08:51.486
Not helpful, right?

00:08:51.486 --> 00:08:53.385
I mean, you didn't find
that helpful answer

00:08:53.385 --> 00:08:56.198
but you're going to control your destiny.

00:08:56.198 --> 00:08:57.198
I'm telling you.

00:08:57.198 --> 00:09:00.187
No one else is going to do it,
not unless you got a rich dad.

00:09:00.187 --> 00:09:03.679
Have you got a rich dad, a rich uncle?

00:09:03.679 --> 00:09:04.689
No, well then that's it.

00:09:04.689 --> 00:09:07.689
You're going to have to do it yourself.

00:09:12.405 --> 00:09:15.154
- The funny thing is
with enough persistence,

00:09:15.154 --> 00:09:19.237
most things that seem
impossible become possible.

00:09:22.498 --> 00:09:27.083
I'm always amazed at how often
you can turn things around

00:09:27.083 --> 00:09:30.750
and people take no for
an answer too easily.

00:09:32.015 --> 00:09:35.162
It's whether you're
trying to achieve a goal

00:09:35.162 --> 00:09:38.075
like get into business school,

00:09:38.075 --> 00:09:40.227
or my Green Card was the same way.

00:09:40.227 --> 00:09:43.042
I left a job that had sponsored me

00:09:43.042 --> 00:09:44.429
but I still got my Green Card

00:09:44.429 --> 00:09:46.926
even though no lawyer would take me.

00:09:46.926 --> 00:09:50.216
I became my own lawyer, got
my Green Card without working

00:09:50.216 --> 00:09:52.799
while I was in business school,

00:09:53.688 --> 00:09:55.319
and I did it perfectly legally.

00:09:55.319 --> 00:09:59.508
My strategy there was if I
could convince immigration

00:09:59.508 --> 00:10:03.675
I'd confuse them and I did,
and they gave me my Green Card.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:10.676
- Trust your gut.

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:12.710
It's so important to trust your gut.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:15.530
I saw a man speak one time

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.346
and he said I'll prove
to you in four words

00:10:17.346 --> 00:10:18.936
there's no such thing as a bad idea

00:10:18.936 --> 00:10:22.603
and he said, "Teenage
Mutant Ninja Turtles."

00:10:24.215 --> 00:10:26.570
So, I'm here today to
prove to you in two words

00:10:26.570 --> 00:10:27.867
there's no such thing as a bad idea

00:10:27.867 --> 00:10:29.823
and that's footless pantyhose.

00:10:29.823 --> 00:10:31.595
So, no matter what your ideas are

00:10:31.595 --> 00:10:34.142
you're doing something
better than your competitors.

00:10:34.142 --> 00:10:35.411
That's why you're a business.

00:10:35.411 --> 00:10:36.517
You've thought of an idea.

00:10:36.517 --> 00:10:37.744
That's why you're here,

00:10:37.744 --> 00:10:41.161
and then be prepared for the opportunity.

00:10:47.717 --> 00:10:49.264
- When you go out into the world

00:10:49.264 --> 00:10:51.566
you should try to stand
up against the trend

00:10:51.566 --> 00:10:54.226
even though it might, literally,
it might cost your job,

00:10:54.226 --> 00:10:55.858
it might cost your promotion,

00:10:55.858 --> 00:10:57.591
but in the end think for yourself.

00:10:57.591 --> 00:10:58.590
Be innovative.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:10:59.423
Try.

00:10:59.423 --> 00:11:00.492
I mean, I'm not telling you to go in

00:11:00.492 --> 00:11:01.480
and tell 'em what to do.

00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:03.031
You've got to be careful
about that obviously,

00:11:03.031 --> 00:11:06.613
but if you have ideas, go slam the table.

00:11:06.613 --> 00:11:07.614
Don't worry about it.

00:11:07.614 --> 00:11:10.447
Come up with your own imagination.

00:11:15.264 --> 00:11:19.480
- To be serious, if you
want to be the next thing

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:21.046
you have to have a very big heart.

00:11:21.046 --> 00:11:25.474
You have to take quite a lot
of risk, calculated risk.

00:11:25.474 --> 00:11:29.233
First of all, you have to
make sure that you are honest.

00:11:29.233 --> 00:11:31.604
You have to make sure you
don't destroy the name

00:11:31.604 --> 00:11:33.161
because your name is very important.

00:11:33.161 --> 00:11:37.449
The most valuable asset
that you have going forward,

00:11:37.449 --> 00:11:39.399
if you don't have a good
name, even the banks,

00:11:39.399 --> 00:11:40.792
it doesn't matter how big you are

00:11:40.792 --> 00:11:42.511
they're not going to touch you,

00:11:42.511 --> 00:11:45.631
so you must make sure they
have a very, very good name

00:11:45.631 --> 00:11:49.381
and number three, you
have to make sure that,

00:11:50.494 --> 00:11:53.262
you see that look, nothing is impossible.

00:11:53.262 --> 00:11:55.373
One you see that yes,
nothing is impossible,

00:11:55.373 --> 00:11:58.272
it means that you can
actually achieve that target.

00:11:58.272 --> 00:11:59.273
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:11:59.273 --> 00:12:00.280
I hope you enjoyed the video.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.902
I'd love to know what did you think of it?

00:12:01.902 --> 00:12:03.959
What was the piece of advice
that you're going to take

00:12:03.959 --> 00:12:05.881
some kind of immediate action on somehow

00:12:05.881 --> 00:12:07.963
in your life or in your business?

00:12:07.963 --> 00:12:09.194
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:12:09.194 --> 00:12:10.311
I'm really curious to find out.

00:12:10.311 --> 00:12:11.457
Thank you guys again for watching.

00:12:11.457 --> 00:12:12.809
I believe in you.

00:12:12.809 --> 00:12:14.957
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:12:14.957 --> 00:12:16.549
and whatever your one word is.

00:12:16.549 --> 00:12:19.049
Much love, I'll see you soon.

